{"kind":"request","text":"S11: one IPv6 /48 cannot fill a shared window table.\n\nTwo checker notes describe one weakness, and this request is my\nruling on both. It is the overflow-key decision that S1-F 17eb790d\nleft to me.\n\n- S1, approval c6fcf62e. The creation table holds 8,192 windows and\n  one address key opens at most 31. About 265 distinct IPv4\n  addresses or IPv6 /64s fill it. Every new identity then shares 10\n  creations an hour.\n- S4, landing check 53e7665c. The control table holds 4,096\n  identities and one address opens at most 120 keys. About 34\n  addresses or /64s fill it, and 34 more fill cleanup. Every new\n  identity then shares 120 calls a minute.\n\nOne /48 holds 65,536 /64s, so one sender with one /48 reaches both\nstates. Members who already hold a window keep it. Newcomers do not\nget one.\n\nWanted, in one head with checker review:\n\n1. A sender inside one IPv6 /48 cannot fill either table. Choose the\n   smallest form. Two candidates: a window for the /48 that bounds\n   how many /64 keys it opens, or an overflow counter keyed by /48\n   in place of the one shared counter. Give your choice and its\n   reason in the note. You need no ruling for it.\n2. For the control table only, consider the checker's other remedy\n   from 6fbde9b8: a key takes a row only after the room's standing\n   check admits its actor. Take it if it is smaller than item 1 for\n   that table. Say which you chose.\n3. Documents. Section 7 of docs/security/entry-points.md and\n   docs/hosted-mcp.md state the new saturation numbers: how many\n   distinct /48s, and how many distinct IPv4 addresses, fill each\n   table. IPv4 stays keyed by address. Say so.\n\nTests, each failing at main 28aa0446:\n\n- Creation: 300 distinct /64s inside one /48 each take a creation\n  window. A creation from an address outside that /48 then succeeds.\n- Control: 40 distinct /64s inside one /48 each open 120 fresh keys.\n  A member's signed create and retire from another prefix then\n  answer 201 and 202.\n\nOrder: after the cutover head, with S10 or beside it. S11 and S10\nboth land before hosted MCP opens on a public host for rooms whose\nmembers we do not know. Neither holds the O4 live window. That\nwindow is supervised, on our own rooms, and a flood there costs a\nretry.\n\nS1-F item 1 still documents the limit as it is today. S11 changes\nthat sentence when it lands.","body":{"conditions":"One head with checker review. Two tests that fail at main 28aa0446: creation and control each survive a flood of /64s from one /48. Docs state the new saturation numbers.","target_head":"28aa0446ab0f5cac2753fa802a186ecb7843daca","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}